12. What is the difference between keyof and typeof?
    Answer:
        const user = {
          name: "Rahul",
          age: 30
        };

        type User = typeof user;
        // { name: string; age: number }

        type UserKeys = keyof User;
        // "name" | "age"

13. What is Type Narrowing?
    Answer:
        जब checks के जरिए किसी broad type को अधिक specific type तक सीमित किया जाता है, उसे narrowing कहते हैं।

            function printValue(value: string | number) {
              if (typeof value === "string") {
                console.log(value.toUpperCase());
              } else {
                console.log(value.toFixed(2));
              }
            }

            printValue("hello"); // HELLO
            printValue(12.5);    // 12.50

14. What are Type Guards?
    Answer:
        Type guard ऐसा check है जो TypeScript को किसी value का type पहचानने में मदद करता है।
            function isString(value: unknown): value is string {
              return typeof value === "string";
            }

            function display(value: unknown) {
              if (isString(value)) {
                console.log(value.toUpperCase());
              }
            }

            यहाँ value is string को type predicate कहते हैं।

15. What are Tuples?
    Answer:
        Tuple एक array-like structure है जिसमें elements के types और positions निर्धारित किए जा सकते हैं।

            let employee: [number, string, boolean];
            employee = [101, "Rahul", true];
            // employee = ["Rahul", 101, true]; // Error

            let user: [string, number, boolean] = ["Amir", 30, true];

            console.log(user[0]); // Amir
            console.log(user[1]); // 30
            console.log(user[2]); // true

16. What are Enums?
    Answer:
        Enums related named constants को group करते हैं।

            enum Direction {
              Up,
              Down,
              Left,
              Right
            }

            const move: Direction = Direction.Up;

            console.log(move); // 0

        String enum का उदाहरण:
            enum Status {
              Pending = "PENDING",
              Success = "SUCCESS"
            }

17. What are Index Signatures?
    Answer:
        जब object में keys dynamic हों और उनका type एक जैसा हो, तब index signature उपयोग कर सकते हैं।

        interface Scores {
          [subject: string]: number;
        }

        const marks: Scores = {
          Maths: 90,
          Science: 85
        };

18. What are Function Overloads?
    Answer:
    -------
        Function overloads से एक ही function के लिए अलग-अलग call signatures define कर सकते हैं।

            function format(value: string): string;
            function format(value: number): string;

            function format(value: string | number): string {
              return String(value);
            }

            format("Hello");
            format(100);

19. What is Structural Typing?
    Answer:
    ------
        TypeScript में objects की compatibility मुख्यतः उनके structure पर आधारित होती है, केवल उनके declared नाम पर नहीं।

            type Person = { name: string };
            const employee = { name: "Rahul", salary: 50000 };
            const person: Person = employee; // Valid

21. What are Utility Types?
    Answer:
    -------
        Utility types मौजूदा types से नए types बनाने में मदद करते हैं।

        interface User {
          id: number;
          name: string;
          email: string;
        }

        type PartialUser = Partial<User>;
        type RequiredUser = Required<PartialUser>;
        type UserPreview = Pick<User, "id" | "name">;
        type UserWithoutEmail = Omit<User, "email">;

22. What are Record, Exclude, Extract, and NonNullable?
    Answer:
    ------
        type Roles = "admin" | "user" | "guest";
        type Permissions = Record<Roles, boolean>;

        type PublicRoles = Exclude<Roles, "admin">;
        // "user" | "guest"

        type SelectedRoles = Extract<Roles, "admin" | "user">;
        // "admin" | "user"

        type Value = NonNullable<string | number | null>;
        // string | number

23. What are Mapped Types?
    Answer:
    -------
        Mapped types किसी existing type की properties पर iterate करके नया type बनाते हैं।

        type ReadonlyType<T> = {
          readonly [K in keyof T]: T[K];
        };

        type User = {
          name: string;
          age: number;
        };

        type ReadonlyUser = ReadonlyType<User>;

24. What are Conditional Types?
    Answer:
    ------
        Conditional types किसी type condition के आधार पर अलग type चुनते हैं।

        type Result<T> = T extends string ? "Text" : "Other";

        type A = Result<string>; // "Text"
        type B = Result<number>; // "Other"

25. What is the infer keyword?
    Answer:
    -------
        infer conditional types के अंदर किसी type का हिस्सा infer करने के लिए उपयोग होता है।

26. What is Declaration Merging?
    Answer:
    -------
        जब TypeScript समान नाम वाले compatible interface declarations को एक declaration में merge करता है, उसे declaration merging कहते हैं।

        interface User {
          name: string;
        }

        interface User {
          age: number;
        }

        const user: User = {
          name: "Rahul",
          age: 30
        };

27. What are .d.ts files?
    Answer:
        Declaration files types की जानकारी देते हैं, बिना implementation code लिखे।

        // greeting.d.ts
        declare function greet(name: string): string;

28. What are Generic Constraints using extends?
    Answer:
    -------
        Generic constraints किसी generic type parameter के लिए requirements तय करते हैं।

        function getLength<T extends { length: number }>(
          value: T
        ): number {
          return value.length;
        }

        getLength("Hello");      // 5
        getLength([1, 2, 3]);    // 3
        // getLength(100);       // Error

29. What are Template Literal Types?
    Answer:
    ------
        Template literal types string literal types को combine करके नए string types बनाते हैं।

        type EventName = "click" | "change";

        type HandlerName = `on${Capitalize<EventName>}`;
        // "onClick" | "onChange"

30. What is the difference between as const and readonly?
    Answer:
        as const किसी literal expression की inferred properties को अधिक specific और readonly बनाता है। readonly किसी property या type की mutability को restrict करता है।

        const config = {
          mode: "production",
          retries: 3
        } as const;

        // config.mode = "development"; // Error
        // config.retries = 5;          // Error

        interface User {
          readonly id: number;
        }